        "math_academy_id": "q-74072",
        "problem": "Find the numbers $c$ such that the average value of $f(x)=3{x}^{2}-24x+23$ on the interval $[0,c]$ is equal to $-12.$",
        "worked_solution": "To solve for $c,$ we apply the average value formula:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{\\text{ave}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -12 & =\\frac{1}{c-0}{\\int }_{0}^{c}(3{x}^{2}-24x+23)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ -12 & ={\\frac{1}{c}({x}^{3}-12{x}^{2}+23x)|}_{0}^{c} \\\\ -12 & =\\frac{1}{c}[({c}^{3}-12{c}^{2}+23c)-0] \\\\ -12 & ={c}^{2}-12c+23 \\\\ 0 & ={c}^{2}-12c+35 \\\\ 0 & =(c-5)(c-7) \\\\ c & =5,\\,7\\end{aligned}\n$$",
